Narrow the dashboard to notifications and the agenda.

The Waybar audio panel now owns Bluetooth and volume, the Wi-Fi button owns
the network, and the dashboard button itself shows the battery, so the
Bluetooth and Do Not Disturb tiles, the volume card and the battery/network
row are all duplicates. Removing them leaves airplane mode, idle inhibit and
the power profile on one row, and the space they used goes to the calendar
and notification lists.

Do Not Disturb keeps its switch inside the notification card. Airplane mode
still turns Bluetooth off and back on; only its tile is gone.

